From: Mirdispo contributors
Subject: Say how many frames were captured and how many were sent

A session reported frames only when it had dropped some, which left the two
rates unsaid the rest of the time. Silence then reads as the rate being the
one the receiver was promised, when it may be anything at all: a desktop with
little moving on it is captured slowly and every frame of it encoded, and
that is the same silence as keeping up at the full rate.

The difference matters for more than the picture. The distance between
keyframes is counted in frames rather than in time, so what it comes to in
seconds depends on a rate nothing was reporting. A link sending two frames a
second puts a keyframe fifteen seconds apart while the setting still reads
thirty.

Both rates are now named every ten seconds, as counts and per second, so what
leaves the encoder is known rather than inferred from what is not said. The
line about frames dropped to keep up is unchanged and still follows when
there were any.

diff -ruN a/src/wfd/wfd-media-factory.c b/src/wfd/wfd-media-factory.c
--- a/src/wfd/wfd-media-factory.c
+++ b/src/wfd/wfd-media-factory.c
@@ -120,12 +120,24 @@
       else if (now >= qos_data->report_at)
         {
           gint captured = g_atomic_int_exchange (&qos_data->frames_in, 0);
+          gint seconds = (gint) (WFD_QOS_REPORT_INTERVAL / GST_SECOND);
+
+          /* Saying only that frames were dropped leaves the two rates
+           * unsaid, and silence then reads as the rate being the one that
+           * was asked for when it may be anything at all: a desktop with
+           * little moving on it is captured slowly, and every frame of it
+           * encoded, which is the same silence as keeping up at full rate.
+           * Both rates are named every time, so what is leaving is known
+           * rather than assumed. */
+          g_message ("WfdMediaFactory: %d frames captured and %u encoded in the last %d s (%.1f and %.1f a second)",
+                     captured, qos_data->frames_out, seconds,
+                     captured / (gdouble) seconds,
+                     qos_data->frames_out / (gdouble) seconds);
 
           /* A couple of frames are always on their way through. */
           if (captured > (gint) qos_data->frames_out + 2)
             g_message ("WfdMediaFactory: %d of %d frames in the last %d s were dropped to keep up",
-                       captured - (gint) qos_data->frames_out, captured,
-                       (gint) (WFD_QOS_REPORT_INTERVAL / GST_SECOND));
+                       captured - (gint) qos_data->frames_out, captured, seconds);
 
           qos_data->frames_out = 0;
           qos_data->report_at = now + WFD_QOS_REPORT_INTERVAL;
